  "id": "Harrow-PL_0472_26",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Conversion of dwelling into two flats (2 x 3 beds); external alterations; separate amenity space; parking; bin / cycle storage",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The cumulative impacts of the proposed car parking space together with bin stores required to serve the development cannot be satisfactorily provided within the front forecourt of the site to meet the Council&#x27;s requirements in respect of the development, and the likely increase in such allocated spaces would leave limited scope for sufficient soft landscaping to mitigate the impact of the development in the wider area. This will result in visual clutter which will be detrimental to the character and appearance of the area. The proposal is therefore contrary to National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 and T6 of The London Plan (2021), and Policies GR1 and M1 of Harrow’s Local Plan (2026).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed subdivision of the existing dwellinghouse into multiple flats would result in an intensified form of residential use that is not considered appropriate having regard to the site’s location and accessibility. In particular, the low PTAL of 1b indicates the site is unsuitable for such intensification.&amp;nbsp; The proposal is there contrary to the spatial objectives of Policy HO2 (1c) of Harrow’s Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
